WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.459 --> 00:00:06.150
Uh, one of the real downsides to having a
president like Donald Trump that throws so

00:00:06.150 --> 00:00:12.230
many norms and conventions to the wind and
acts in the childish, immature and erratic

00:00:12.230 --> 00:00:19.050
way that he does is that it can help normalize
or rehabilitate former presidents who also

00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:20.939
did things that aren't particularly good.

00:00:20.939 --> 00:00:24.140
And I've been really careful to avoid this
with George W. Bush.

00:00:24.140 --> 00:00:30.339
So for the last two and a half years when
I've pointed out, wow, Trump is going beyond

00:00:30.339 --> 00:00:33.910
even the craziness of George W. Bush in many
ways.

00:00:33.910 --> 00:00:38.449
I'm always sort of careful to remind you that
we don't want to incorrectly rehabilitate

00:00:38.449 --> 00:00:40.390
George W Bush's image.

00:00:40.390 --> 00:00:48.480
Bush was a terrible ignorant neo-con as a
president, but he had some common decency

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:53.510
in some basic human ways that Donald Trump
just completely lacks.

00:00:53.510 --> 00:00:58.199
And in the same way, I had many disagreements
with Barack Obama on policy during the eight

00:00:58.199 --> 00:01:00.710
years of Barack Obama's presidency.

00:01:00.710 --> 00:01:06.000
Obama's escalation of the drone war, Obama's
war on whistle blowers, Obama's inability

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:12.250
to make real progress on immigration, uh,
Obama starting from to make a position on

00:01:12.250 --> 00:01:14.060
healthcare reform.

00:01:14.060 --> 00:01:19.200
There's a very long list of disagreements
I had on policy with Barack Obama, but Barack

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:24.140
Obama was an intelligent, thoughtful, and
to my belief, fundamentally genuine person

00:01:24.140 --> 00:01:30.240
to the extent that you can know those characteristics
about a person when you see them through the

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:33.549
media and through their actions as president
of the United States.

00:01:33.549 --> 00:01:39.270
And Barack Obama recently wrote a letter in
response to the shootings in El Paso and in

00:01:39.270 --> 00:01:43.950
Dayton, Ohio, and it is just a glaring reminder
of what we're lacking right now, which is

00:01:43.950 --> 00:01:50.880
a president who behaves like an adult and
Donald Trump couldn't take it and was so triggered

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:55.840
by Barack Obama that even though Obama didn't
mention him in his letter, Trump immediately

00:01:55.840 --> 00:01:58.060
took to Twitter to insult Barack Obama.

00:01:58.060 --> 00:02:00.729
Now this is no Obama love letter.

00:02:00.729 --> 00:02:01.729
Okay?

00:02:01.729 --> 00:02:06.450
It's just something that reminded me of what
we've lost with Donald Trump is president.

00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:10.111
Let's take a look at the letter, which most
importantly for me points out some of the

00:02:10.111 --> 00:02:14.330
obvious things that a president should be
saying, but Donald Trump is not Obama saying,

00:02:14.330 --> 00:02:18.590
quote, Michelle and I grieve with all the
families in El Paso in Dayton, who endured

00:02:18.590 --> 00:02:20.230
these latest mass shootings.

00:02:20.230 --> 00:02:24.360
Even if details are still emerging, there
are a few things we already know to be true.

00:02:24.360 --> 00:02:30.150
First, no other nation on earth comes close
to experiencing the frequency of mass shootings

00:02:30.150 --> 00:02:32.020
that we see in the United States.

00:02:32.020 --> 00:02:36.030
No other developed nation tolerates the levels
of gun violence that we do.

00:02:36.030 --> 00:02:39.671
Every time this happens, we're told that tougher
gun laws won't stop all murders, that they

00:02:39.671 --> 00:02:43.640
won't stop every deranged individual from
getting a weapon and shooting innocent people

00:02:43.640 --> 00:02:45.060
in public places.

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:48.040
But the evidence shows that they can stop
some killings.

00:02:48.040 --> 00:02:50.200
They can save some families from heartbreak.

00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:54.860
We are not helpless here, and until all of
us stand up and insist on holding public officials

00:02:54.860 --> 00:02:59.220
accountable for changing our gun laws, these
tragedies will keep happening.

00:02:59.220 --> 00:03:04.051
Second, while the motivations behind these
shootings may not yet be fully known, there

00:03:04.051 --> 00:03:08.870
are indications that the El Paso shooting
follows a dangerous trend, troubled individuals

00:03:08.870 --> 00:03:14.840
who embrace racist ideologies and see themselves
obligated to act violently to preserve white

00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:19.900
supremacy like the followers of Isis and other
foreign terrorist organizations.

00:03:19.900 --> 00:03:25.620
These individuals may act alone, but they've
been radicalized by white nationalists websites

00:03:25.620 --> 00:03:27.550
that proliferate on the internet.

00:03:27.550 --> 00:03:32.210
That means that both law enforcement agencies
and internet platforms need to come up with

00:03:32.210 --> 00:03:36.430
better strategies to reduce the influence
of these hate groups.

00:03:36.430 --> 00:03:41.670
But just as important, all of us have to send
a clarion call and behave with the values

00:03:41.670 --> 00:03:45.720
of and diversity that should be the hallmark
of our democracy.

00:03:45.720 --> 00:03:50.150
We should soundly reject language coming out
of the mouths of any of our leaders that feeds

00:03:50.150 --> 00:03:54.150
a climate of fear and hatred or normalizes
racist sentiments.

00:03:54.150 --> 00:03:58.400
Leaders who demonize those who don't look
like us or suggest that other people, including

00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:03.510
immigrants, threaten our way of life or refer
to other people as subhuman or imply that

00:04:03.510 --> 00:04:06.510
America belongs to just one certain type of
people.

00:04:06.510 --> 00:04:07.780
Such language isn't new.

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:11.970
It's been at the root of most human tragedy
throughout history here in America and around

00:04:11.970 --> 00:04:12.970
the world.

00:04:12.970 --> 00:04:17.849
It's at the root of slavery and Jim Crow,
the Holocaust, the genocide in Rwanda and

00:04:17.849 --> 00:04:20.139
ethnic cleansing in the Balkans.

00:04:20.139 --> 00:04:25.139
It has no place in our politics and our public
life, and it's time for the overwhelming majority

00:04:25.139 --> 00:04:30.819
of Americans of goodwill, of every race and
faith and political party to say as much,

00:04:30.819 --> 00:04:32.780
clearly and unequivocally.

00:04:32.780 --> 00:04:36.229
This is just obvious contexts that's missing.

00:04:36.229 --> 00:04:40.840
When we hear Republicans and Trump talk about
this, no other country has these gun violence

00:04:40.840 --> 00:04:41.840
problems.

00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:47.449
No other country country has the resistance
caused by stupid but well-funded talking points

00:04:47.449 --> 00:04:48.479
that we do.

00:04:48.479 --> 00:04:53.509
And secondly, whether it's isis or these right
wing terrorists, it's the same mechanism of

00:04:53.509 --> 00:04:58.030
radicalization and we have to call it out
as such, and we have to call it terrorism

00:04:58.030 --> 00:04:59.110
in all cases.

00:04:59.110 --> 00:05:06.020
And by the way, just dripping from the letter
is actual empathy and Constellation for people.

00:05:06.020 --> 00:05:09.240
Something that Donald Trump seems fundamentally
just unable to achieve.

00:05:09.240 --> 00:05:13.979
Instead of having the instincts of going to
Puerto Rico after a hurricane and shooting

00:05:13.979 --> 00:05:17.669
rolls of paper towels like basketball's like
a game.

00:05:17.669 --> 00:05:22.080
And Donald Trump was so triggered by this
letter, which doesn't even mention him by

00:05:22.080 --> 00:05:26.889
name, that he immediately went to Twitter
to insult Barack Obama with a quote from Fox

00:05:26.889 --> 00:05:31.670
and friends quoting Brian Kilmeade on Fox
and friends saying, did George Bush ever condemn

00:05:31.670 --> 00:05:34.500
President Obama after Sandy Hook?

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:38.219
President Obama had 32 mass shootings during
his reign.

00:05:38.219 --> 00:05:41.070
Not many people said Obama's out of control.

00:05:41.070 --> 00:05:45.819
Mass shootings were happening before the president
even thought about running for president.

00:05:45.819 --> 00:05:50.020
Now there's a number of problems with that,
including that there have been hundreds and

00:05:50.020 --> 00:05:52.569
hundreds of mass shootings under Donald Trump.

00:05:52.569 --> 00:05:57.849
But more importantly, Obama didn't even mention
Trump in his letter, and Obama was trying

00:05:57.849 --> 00:06:02.650
to make changes, which he couldn't get done
as simple as background checks.

00:06:02.650 --> 00:06:06.999
And this goes to Donald Trump's insecurity
more than anything else.

00:06:06.999 --> 00:06:08.199
And there's two sides to this.

00:06:08.199 --> 00:06:12.710
On the one hand, just being able to speak
and write in complete sentences distinguishes

00:06:12.710 --> 00:06:16.250
Barack Obama from Donald Trump in really important
ways.

00:06:16.250 --> 00:06:21.029
But the substance of the letter is also something
that Donald Trump is unwilling or unable to

00:06:21.029 --> 00:06:22.029
put together.

00:06:22.029 --> 00:06:24.470
I've said before, money can't buy class.

00:06:24.470 --> 00:06:26.370
It's never been more clear than right now.

00:06:26.370 --> 00:06:31.360
But the problem is that the longer Trump is
in office, the longer that this becomes more

00:06:31.360 --> 00:06:33.000
and more okay.

00:06:33.000 --> 00:06:39.199
It shouldn't be startling to us to see, oh,
a president that can speak coherently and

00:06:39.199 --> 00:06:44.479
isn't personally attacking political enemies
on Twitter and is thinking big picture about

00:06:44.479 --> 00:06:46.350
social and political issues.

00:06:46.350 --> 00:06:47.500
It does surprise us.

00:06:47.500 --> 00:06:50.870
It's notable even for me and for people in
our audience.

00:06:50.870 --> 00:06:54.800
Trump has been normalized to a great degree
and every day that he's in office becomes

00:06:54.800 --> 00:06:55.800
more normal.

00:06:55.800 --> 00:07:00.879
In a sense, there has to be a purge that's
bigger than just getting rid of Trump.

00:07:00.879 --> 00:07:05.409
Having people like Jared and Ivanka in positions
of power has been normalized.

00:07:05.409 --> 00:07:08.820
Having advisors like Kellyanne Conway has
been normalized.

00:07:08.820 --> 00:07:13.430
Treating our allies with disrespect as some
show of manhood has been normalized.

00:07:13.430 --> 00:07:15.440
It all has to be purged.

00:07:15.440 --> 00:07:20.480
It only starts with getting Trump out in November
of 2020 let me know what you think.

